HelSpin — third-party components
================================

HelSpin depends on the following, each under its own licence. Their terms
govern their own code and are not altered by HelSpin's licence.

PySide6 / Qt          LGPL v3 (also available under GPL and commercially)
                      https://www.qt.io/licensing
                      Qt is used as a shared library and is NOT statically
                      linked, so a recipient may replace it with a modified
                      build. Source for the Qt version distributed with a
                      HelSpin binary is available from the Qt Project, and
                      on request from the HelSpin authors.

nmrglue               New BSD (3-clause)
numpy                 BSD 3-clause
scipy                 BSD 3-clause. Binary builds bundle OpenBLAS (BSD
                      3-clause), libgfortran (GPL v3 WITH GCC Runtime Library
                      Exception, which permits use in non-GPL programs) and
                      libquadmath (LGPL v2.1, dynamically linked).
matplotlib            Matplotlib licence (PSF-style, BSD-compatible). Bundles
                      fonts under OFL-1.1 and the BaKoMa font licence.

Full licence texts are installed alongside each package and can be printed
with:

    python -m pip show -f <package>

If HelSpin is redistributed as a bundled installer, that bundle MUST be built
one-directory (not one-file) so the Qt libraries remain replaceable, and must
ship this NOTICE and the LGPL text. See docs in HANDOFF.md.
